# Copy to .env.local (gitignored) and fill in. These are the five values
# that cannot be committed; every other setting has a default baked into
# the image, or a flag on the CLI.
#
# One file, both consumers: mise.toml loads it via `_.file` for the host
# tooling (`just sync`, `just auth`) and compose.yaml loads it as its only
# env_file for the container. That is the point — two copies of a
# credential drift, and the one that drifts is discovered at the worst
# moment.
#
# Keep it to secrets. Non-secret settings belong in the environment: the
# Dockerfile's ENV block for image defaults, compose.yaml's `environment:`
# for a deployment, mise.toml for the host toolchain.
#
# Restrict it once you have filled it in:
#
#     chmod 600 .env.local
#
# Nothing does this for you, and the default umask leaves it 0644. The
# database and the backup snapshots are both created 0600 because they
# hold the Spotify refresh token; this file holds that token's client
# secret plus the DI.fm key, so leaving it world-readable undoes that.
#
# Capture DIFMSYNC_API_KEY / DIFMSYNC_MEMBER_ID per docs/difm-api.md.
# DIFMSYNC_API_KEY is long-lived and has no rotation path — treat it as a
# shared-fate secret. No DI.fm password is needed at any point.
DIFMSYNC_API_KEY=
DIFMSYNC_MEMBER_ID=
DIFMSYNC_SPOTIFY_CLIENT_ID=
DIFMSYNC_SPOTIFY_CLIENT_SECRET=
DIFMSYNC_PLAYLIST_ID=

# Only needed to reach the consent flow from somewhere other than a
# browser on the Docker host. The image already points this at the
# consent port compose publishes (http://127.0.0.1:3437/callback), which
# is enough to authorize locally or through an SSH tunnel — Spotify
# accepts a loopback literal over plain HTTP, so nothing has to terminate
# TLS for it.
#
# Anything else must be HTTPS, which means a proxy in front: see the
# authorizing section of docs/deploy.md. Whatever you set must match a
# redirect URI registered in the Spotify dashboard exactly. Both consent
# routes and the `auth` listener's address are derived from it.
#
# `difmsync auth --manual` needs none of this — it never listens, so the
# redirect URI only has to be registered, not reachable.
# DIFMSYNC_SPOTIFY_REDIRECT_URL=https://<node>.<tailnet>.ts.net/difmsync/callback
